5. Technical Stack
5.1 Web Frontend
•	Framework: React with Vite
•	Location: /web directory in servio_dev repository
•	State management: React hooks — no Redux in V1
•	HTTP client: axios or fetch — consistent choice per session
•	Routing: React Router v6
•	Icons: Tabler Icons (ti-*) — outline only, never filled variants
•	Fonts: DM Sans + Playfair Display — loaded from Google Fonts

5.2 Mobile Frontend
•	Framework: Expo React Native
•	Build sequence: mobile starts after web Phase A is stable
•	Design system: same colours, typography, and layout patterns as web
•	Same backend API — no separate mobile endpoints

5.3 Backend API
•	Base URL (emulator): http://127.0.0.1:5001/servio-dev-55d2d/asia-south1/api
•	Authentication: Firebase Auth token in Authorization header
•	All role-protected routes require verifyToken + verifyRole middleware
•	Tokens expire after 1 hour — re-login required per test session

6. Frontend Development Rules
6.1 Design Rules
•	Never deviate from the locked colour palette — see Section 2
•	Never add credentials or branding to the top bar — Servio name only
•	Never show a role switcher in the UI — each user has one role
•	Home screen must remain clean — maximum 3 stat cards + 1 CTA + 2 small panels
•	Order Now CTA appears on home screen for employee role only

6.2 Build Rules
•	Build Phase A screens fully before starting Phase B
•	Each screen must be tested against the backend emulator before moving to the next
•	No UI improvisation — if a field is not in the schema, it does not appear on screen
•	Mobile build starts only after all Phase A web screens are validated

6.3 Support Contact Flow
•	Support icon sits on the right side of the bottom strip
•	Clicking it opens a small popup containing manager contact number and tenant support email
•	These values are read from appSettings collection in Firestore — not hardcoded
•	Admin updates them via the Contact Us screen (Screen 19)
•	Developer contact is never shown in the app

6.4 Deferred Features — Do Not Build in V1
•	Kiosk / touch screen ordering — parked to V3
•	Interactive menu with dish photos — parked to V3
•	photoUrl and itemDescription on menu items — parked to V3
•	Cafe, tuck shop, bakery, BBQ screens — parked to V1.1 and V1.2
•	SMS, email, WhatsApp notifications — parked to V3

7. Parked Decisions Log
Feature	Target Version	Notes
Kiosk / touch screen ordering	V3	McDonald-style, tablet/large screen, standalone deployment
Interactive menu — dish photos	V3	photoUrl + itemDescription fields added to menuItems at V3
Cafe / TuckShop screens	V1.1	Requires family member flow first
Bakery screens	V1.1	Alongside cafe flow
BBQ screens	V1.2	After V1.1 stable
Cafe/Bakery/BBQ kitchen dashboards	V1.1 / V1.2	Follow their operational flows
SMS/email/WhatsApp notifications	V3	V1 is in-app only
GuestHouse, BOQ, Library	V2	Post V1 launch
Sports, Safety	V3	Post V2
Recipe, Inventory, Procurement	V4	Requires stable operational base
Multiple roles per user	V2+	V1 is single role only — schema change required


